@startuml forbidden-request
title Forbidden request: Bob tries to read Alice's record
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
actor Bob
participant BasicAuthenticationFilter as Basic
participant ExceptionTranslationFilter as Exceptions
participant AuthorizationFilter as URL
participant "Method security\n@PreAuthorize" as Method
participant OwnRecordGuard as Guard
participant "AuthorizationEventPublisher" as Events
participant ApiAccessDeniedHandler as Handler
Bob -> Basic : GET /api/patients/1/record\nvalid bob credentials
Basic -> Basic : authenticate (PATIENT, patientId=2)
Basic -> Exceptions : chain.doFilter
Exceptions -> URL : chain.doFilter
URL -> Method : PATIENT role passes
Method -> Guard : allows(authentication, 1)
Guard --> Method : false (2 != 1)
Method -> Events : AuthorizationDeniedEvent\nobject: MethodInvocation
note right of Events
  Delivered to the audit listener;
  persistence implemented in slice 3.
end note
Method --> Exceptions : AccessDeniedException
note over Method, Guard
  Controller body and repository never run.
end note
Exceptions -> Handler : authenticated caller: handle(...)
Handler -> Handler : ApiError.write(..., 403, "Forbidden", request)
Handler --> Bob : 403 application/json\n{"status":403,"error":"Forbidden","path":"/api/patients/1/record"}
note over URL, Events
  Pure role denial: nurse POST /api/patients/1/prescriptions
  AuthorizationFilter refuses the DOCTOR requirement,
  publishes AuthorizationDeniedEvent (object: HttpServletRequest),
  and throws before method security. Same handler returns 403.
end note
@enduml
